      "answer": "Ambessa is a fighter and assassin who combines physical ability damage with empowered attacks that restore energy. Her ability-linked dashes let her reposition, but cannot cross terrain or occur while immobilized or grounded. Her ultimate blinks her to the farthest enemy champion in a chosen line.",
      "build_focus": "AD",
      "card_id": "champ:ambessa:overview:L1",
      "counterplay": "Limit her access to attacks and use grounding or immobilization to restrict her dashes.",
      "facts": [
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "Name: Ambessa. Official role tags: Fighter, Assassin.",
              "source_id": "riot:role"
            },
            {
              "quote": "Active: Ambessa slashes with her twin drakehounds in the target direction, dealing physical damage to enemies hit.",
              "source_id": "wiki:cunningsweep"
            },
            {
              "quote": "Medarda Maxim: Ambessa's next basic attack gains range, bonus attack speed, deals bonus physical damage, and restores energy.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "Ambessa is a fighter and assassin who combines physical ability damage with empowered attacks that restore energy."
        },
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "Entering an attack or movement command while casting an ability will cause Ambessa to dash a short distance once the ability is cast",
              "source_id": "riot:P"
            },
            {
              "quote": "This dash cannot pass through terrain.Ambessa cannot dash while immobilized or grounded.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "Her ability-linked dashes let her reposition, but cannot cross terrain or occur while immobilized or grounded."
        },
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "Ambessa blinks to the farthest enemy champion in a line of her choosing and suppresses them upon her arrival.",
              "source_id": "riot:R"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "Her ultimate blinks her to the farthest enemy champion in a chosen line."
        }
      ],
      "priority": "A",
      "priority_reason": "Her attack cycle and mobility limits shape engagements.",
      "uncertainties": []
    },
    {
      "answer": "An attack or movement command during an ability's brief action lockout queues a dash toward that target or location afterward; the dash cannot cross terrain or occur while immobilized or grounded. Ability casts grant temporary Medarda Maxim stacks, up to three; basic attacks consume one each for extra range, attack speed, physical damage, and energy restoration. Ambessa sees her dash direction and destination indicator, and her empowered-attack pips are visible only to her player.",
      "build_focus": "",
      "card_id": "champ:ambessa:system:p:drakehoundsstep:recognize:L2",
      "counterplay": "Deny attack access to limit energy restoration, and use grounding or immobilization to restrict repositioning.",
      "facts": [
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "During the lockout of Ambessa's abilities, inputting an attack or movement command causes her to dash to or towards the target or location, respectively, after the lockout ends.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            },
            {
              "quote": "This dash cannot pass through terrain.Ambessa cannot dash while immobilized or grounded.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "An attack or movement command during an ability's brief action lockout queues a dash toward that target or location afterward; the dash cannot cross terrain or occur while immobilized or grounded."
        },
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "Casting an ability generates a stack of Medarda Maxim for a few seconds, up to 3 stacks. Basic attacks consume one stack to become empowered.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            },
            {
              "quote": "Medarda Maxim: Ambessa's next basic attack gains range, bonus attack speed, deals bonus physical damage, and restores energy.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "Ability casts grant temporary Medarda Maxim stacks, up to three; basic attacks consume one each for extra range, attack speed, physical damage, and energy restoration."
        },
        {
          "basis": "source_assertion",
          "citations": [
            {
              "quote": "During Drakehound's Step, a visual indicator is visible to Ambessa displaying the eventual dash's direction and destination location.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            },
            {
              "quote": "The number of available attacks empowered by Medarda Maxim are visible as pips under Ambessa's health bar, only visible to the player.",
              "source_id": "wiki:drakehoundsstep"
            }
          ],
          "claim": "Ambessa sees her dash direction and destination indicator, and her empowered-attack pips are visible only to her player."
        }
      ],
      "priority": "A",
      "priority_reason": "Her dashes and empowered attacks connect repositioning with energy recovery.",
      "uncertainties": [
        "The frozen core describes both indicators as private, but the supplied evidence explicitly establishes exclusivity only for empowered-attack pips. Dash-indicator visibility is retained without inventing exclusivity.",
        "Later commands can replace or cancel the queued dash input.",
        "Immobilization or grounding during an ability lockout can cancel the buffered dash even if the control ends before the dash could begin."
      ]
    },
